- Unknown prices remain `NULL`/unknown, not zero.
- Only an authoritative source may populate `max_regulated_price_egp`.
- Legacy medicine records are not marked verified without evidence.
- Unknown prescription classification fails closed wherever the application must decide whether a prescription is required.
- Database defaults, seed queries, application parsing, TypeScript types, and UI rendering agree on unknown values.
- Existing valid explicit classifications are not overwritten by guessed values.
- Seed behavior is deterministic, idempotent, and non-destructive.

Pay particular attention to `prescription_required` and `requires_prescription`: verify their distinct meanings and mappings instead of assuming they are interchangeable.

Do not fabricate data to make catalog cards look complete.

